.TH ARALERT 1 "November 2026" "ARALert" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aralert \- administrative scripts for installing and operating ARALert
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo scripts/aralert-install.sh
.RI [ SOURCE_DIR ]
.PP
.B sudo scripts/aralert-maintenance.sh
.RB { \-\-on | \-\-off | \-\-status }
.PP
.B sudo scripts/aralert-pause.sh
.RB { \-\-pause | \-\-resume | \-\-status }
.PP
.B sudo scripts/aralert-start-stop.sh
.RB { \-\-start | \-\-stop | \-\-restart }
.PP
.B sudo scripts/aralert-status.sh
.RI [ \-\-save
.IR FILE ]
.PP
.B sudo scripts/aralert-update.sh
.I UPDATE_DIR
.PP
.B sudo scripts/aralert-update.sh
.B \-\-simulate-broken
.SH DESCRIPTION
The ARALert scripts install and administer the ARALert application on Ubuntu or WSL.
All scripts accept
.B \-\-help
and must be run with root privileges.
.TP
.B aralert-install.sh
Creates the protected configuration file, installs dependencies, copies the source tree,
configures PostgreSQL, Gunicorn, systemd, and Nginx, and verifies application health.
.TP
.B aralert-maintenance.sh
Turns maintenance mode on or off, or reports its status.
.TP
.B aralert-pause.sh
Suspends or resumes ARALert processes with POSIX stop and continue signals.
.TP
.B aralert-start-stop.sh
Starts, stops, or restarts PostgreSQL, ARALert, and Nginx in service-safe order.
.TP
.B aralert-status.sh
Reports service state, listening ports, process usage, system resources, and backend health.
Use
.B \-\-save FILE
to save and display the report.
.TP
.B aralert-update.sh
Backs up the database and application, applies an update directory, restarts the service,
and verifies backend health.
.B \-\-simulate-broken
creates a controlled failed-update demonstration and does not require an update directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/aralert/aralert.conf
Root-only installation configuration and generated database and secret values.
.TP
.I /opt/aralert
Installed application directory.
.TP
.I /var/backups/aralert
Database dumps and pre-update archives.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Scripts return zero on success. Nonzero values indicate usage errors, privilege errors,
missing configuration or dependencies, or failed service operations.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
sudo scripts/aralert-install.sh ..
sudo scripts/aralert-status.sh
sudo scripts/aralert-maintenance.sh --on
sudo scripts/aralert-maintenance.sh --off
sudo scripts/aralert-update.sh /tmp/aralert-update
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR nginx (8),
.BR gunicorn (1),
.BR psql (1)
